// pfodWeb NOTE: excludes GPIO4 (IR transmitter), GPIO15/17/21 (LCD SPI
// bus), GPIO16/33/34 (LCD backlight/DC/RST, not exposed in this boards
// own pins_arduino.h) - confirmed via M5Stack AtomS3 docs.
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO41 tagged "button" - confirmed onboard physical
// button via M5Stack M5Unified library source (github.com/m5stack/
// M5Unified, M5Unified.cpp, board_M5AtomS3 case: pinMode(GPIO_NUM_41,
// INPUT)). Onboard NeoPixel RGB LED is on GPIO35 (this board's own
// pins_arduino.h PIN_RGB_LED, confirmed same in M5Unified source) but
// GPIO35 is NOT tagged - it falls in the chip-level pin-exclusion range
// (GPIO33-37 octal flash/PSRAM, see esp32s3/board.json) and has no
// chipGpios entry here; re-adding it would reverse a pre-existing
// exclusion, out of scope for this task. See boardsDetails notes.txt.
